<refentry id="report-geoip.conf" conditional="HAVE_LIBCURL"
          xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <refentryinfo>
    <title>report-geoip.conf</title>
    <productname>systemd</productname>
  </refentryinfo>

  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>report-geoip.conf</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>5</manvolnum>
  </refmeta>

  <refnamediv>
    <refname>report-geoip.conf</refname>
    <refname>report-geoip.conf.d</refname>
    <refpurpose>GeoIP report metrics configuration file</refpurpose>
  </refnamediv>

  <refsynopsisdiv>
    <para><simplelist>
      <member><filename>/etc/systemd/report-geoip.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/run/systemd/report-geoip.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/usr/local/lib/systemd/report-geoip.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/usr/lib/systemd/report-geoip.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/etc/systemd/report-geoip.conf.d/*.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/run/systemd/report-geoip.conf.d/*.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/usr/local/lib/systemd/report-geoip.conf.d/*.conf</filename></member>
      <member><filename>/usr/lib/systemd/report-geoip.conf.d/*.conf</filename></member>
    </simplelist></para>
  </refsynopsisdiv>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Description</title>

    <para>This file configures the behavior of
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-report-geoip@.service</refentrytitle><manvolnum>8</manvolnum></citerefentry>,
    a metrics source for
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd-report</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>
    reporting the approximate geographic location of the system.</para>
  </refsect1>

  <xi:include href="standard-conf.xml" xpointer="main-conf" />

  <refsect1>
    <title>Options</title>

    <para>All options are configured in the [GeoIP] section:</para>

    <variablelist class='config-directives'>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><varname>Endpoint=</varname></term>

        <listitem><para>The HTTP or HTTPS URL of the geolocation web service to query. The service must
        answer a GET request with a JSON object in the format of the
        <ulink url="https://reallyfreegeoip.org/">reallyfreegeoip.org</ulink> service, describing the
        location of the address the request originates from. If assigned the empty string, the default is
        restored. The default is chosen at compile time.</para>

        <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v262"/>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>

      <varlistentry>
        <term><varname>RefreshSec=</varname></term>

        <listitem><para>Controls how often the geolocation data is refreshed from the endpoint, at most.
        Takes a time span, see
        <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.time</refentrytitle><manvolnum>7</manvolnum></citerefentry> for
        details. The acquired data is cached locally, and the endpoint is only contacted again once the
        cached data is older than the specified time. If set to zero, the endpoint is contacted on every
        request. If set to <literal>infinity</literal>, the endpoint is contacted only once, and the cached
        data is used from then on. Defaults to <literal>30min</literal>.</para>

        <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v262"/>
        </listitem>
      </varlistentry>
    </variablelist>

    <para>Use <programlisting>systemd-analyze cat-config systemd/report-geoip.conf</programlisting>
    to display the full config.</para>
  </refsect1>

  <refsect1>
    <title>See Also</title>
